# ===========================================================================
# ltop WinGet manifest — DISABLED TEMPLATE (not submittable as-is)
#
# This file is intentionally named `pauldckim.ltop.0.1.0.yaml.template`
# (not `.yaml`) so that winget tooling and the microsoft/winget-pkgs
# validation pipeline never pick it up.
#
# Format: **singleton** manifest (all fields in one document), current
# WinGet schema v1.12.0:
#   https://aka.ms/winget-manifest.singleton.1.12.0.schema.json
# (The same fields can alternatively be split into the multi-file
# version/locale/installer set — `ManifestType: version` / `locale` /
# `installer` — per current winget-pkgs convention; the installer
# manifest then carries `InstallerType`, `NestedInstallerType` and
# `NestedInstallerFiles` at the root, as in the official
# `Docker.DockerCLI` package.)
#
# Installer route: **portable ZIP** — supported by the official schema:
#   InstallerType: zip
#   NestedInstallerType: portable
#   NestedInstallerFiles:
#     - RelativeFilePath: <path inside the zip>
#       PortableCommandAlias: ltop
# `RelativeFilePath` is relative to the zip root (it includes the
# archive's top-level directory). winget extracts the zip and registers
# the alias; no installer database, no elevation.
#
# Why it is not submittable TODAY (practical blockers, NOT schema rules —
# the schema accepts an unsigned zip/portable manifest):
#   1. The public release URL does not exist yet. The repository and the
#      v0.1.0 GitHub Release (with the archive as an asset) are staged but
#      not published, so `InstallerUrl` would 404. WinGet URL policy
#      requires the InstallerUrl to come directly from the publisher's
#      release location (third-party redirectors are rejected); a GitHub
#      Releases download URL under the publisher's own repository is the
#      publisher's release location — GitHub's internal 302 to its own
#      asset CDN is expected and does not violate the policy.
#   2. The 0.1.0 Windows binary is NOT Authenticode-signed. An unsigned
#      portable exe may be flagged by antivirus/SmartScreen during
#      winget-pkgs review. Signing is the planned mitigation (see
#      ../../docs/DISTRIBUTION.md §4); a self-signed certificate does not
#      satisfy public SmartScreen trust.
#   3. `InstallerSha256` below is the hash of the currently STAGED archive
#      (pinned in releases/v0.1.0/SHA256SUMS). Re-verify it against the
#      published release asset before submission.
#
# To submit (future):
#   - publish the repository and the v0.1.0 release with the archive asset,
#   - rename this file to `pauldckim.ltop.0.1.0.yaml` under
#     `manifests/p/pauldckim/ltop/0.1.0/` in a clone of
#     microsoft/winget-pkgs (or promote it to the multi-file set),
#   - re-verify the hash against the published asset,
#   - run `winget validate` against the manifest schema,
#   - open a pull request at https://github.com/microsoft/winget-pkgs.
# ===========================================================================
# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://aka.ms/winget-manifest.singleton.1.12.0.schema.json
PackageIdentifier: pauldckim.ltop
PackageVersion: 0.1.0
PackageLocale: en-US
Publisher: pauldckim
PackageName: ltop
PackageUrl: https://github.com/pauldckim/ltop-release
License: Proprietary freeware (free use and unmodified redistribution; no sale, no modification, no reverse engineering)
LicenseUrl: https://github.com/pauldckim/ltop-release/blob/main/LICENSE.md
ShortDescription: Single-binary TUI monitor for llama.cpp llama-server and its local process
Description: >-
  ltop is a single-binary, keyboard-only terminal dashboard that monitors a
  local llama.cpp llama-server and the OS process behind it, read-only. It
  polls the server's /metrics, /slots and /props endpoints plus local
  process CPU/memory. Proprietary freeware: free to use and to redistribute
  unmodified; no sale, no modification, no reverse engineering. Source code
  is not published.
ReleaseNotesUrl: https://github.com/pauldckim/ltop-release/releases/tag/v0.1.0
Platform:
  - Windows.Desktop
MinimumOSVersion: 10.0.17763.0
InstallerType: zip
NestedInstallerType: portable
NestedInstallerFiles:
  - RelativeFilePath: ltop-v0.1.0-windows-x86_64/ltop.exe
    PortableCommandAlias: ltop
Installers:
  - Architecture: x64
    # GitHub Releases asset URL under the publisher's own repository — the
    # publisher's release location per WinGet URL policy (GitHub's internal
    # 302 to its asset CDN is expected, not a third-party redirector). The
    # archive is staged locally (dist/v0.1.0/) and will be published as a
    # release asset; the URL becomes reachable once published.
    InstallerUrl: https://github.com/pauldckim/ltop-release/releases/download/v0.1.0/ltop-v0.1.0-windows-x86_64.zip
    # SHA-256 of the staged ltop-v0.1.0-windows-x86_64.zip (pinned in
    # releases/v0.1.0/SHA256SUMS); re-verify against the published asset.
    InstallerSha256: 56731ea57a8aff8f8ffc07229aedb9810b6f7e534def0f7ea26ccd4228dab572
    Scope: user
    UpgradeBehavior: install
ReleaseDate: '2026-09-05'
ManifestType: singleton
ManifestVersion: 1.12.0
